# The secret check, and the list of what it lets pass, need the maintainer's
# review. A pull request's check runs that pull request's own copy of these
# files, so without a reviewer a pull request could widen what passes or switch
# its own check off and still show green. GitHub enforces this only while
# "Require review from Code Owners" is on for main.
/.secrets.baseline @VyLoneReaz
# All of .github/, not only secrets.yml: a new workflow with a job named
# like the secret check could stand in for it as a required check, and a
# local action under .github/actions/ would run code before the scan.
/.github/ @VyLoneReaz
/scripts/secret-scan.py @VyLoneReaz
